# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Fresh_Approch — local configuration
#
#  Copy this file to  .env  in the same folder and fill in the values.
#  .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
#  The servers read it at startup with a built-in loader — no npm
#  install and no dotenv package required.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ManipalCigna API gateway credential.
# This is the base64 blob that follows the word "Basic " in the
# Authorization header. It decodes to a client_id:client_secret pair,
# so treat it as a real secret.
MC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ManipalCigna payload encryption key — exactly 16 characters (AES-128-ECB).
MC_AES_KEY=

# Optional. Only set this if ManipalCigna moves the gateway host.
# MC_GATEWAY=https://online.gateway.manipalcigna.com

# Set to 1 to enable /decrypt and /api/decrypt-test on port 3003.
# These expose the AES key as a decryption oracle to anything that can reach
# the port — leave off unless you are actively reverse-engineering a payload.
# MC_ENABLE_DECRYPT_TOOLS=1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Production deployment only (e.g. Webuzo) — leave all of these unset
#  for local use.
#
#  Only mc_server.js actually loads this .env file. care_server.js,
#  niva_server.js and sh_server.js read PORT/PUBLIC_ORIGIN_* straight from
#  the real process environment instead — on a host like Webuzo you set
#  them per app in the panel's own "Environment Variables" field, not by
#  shipping a .env file for them. Unset anywhere, every server falls back
#  to today's exact http://localhost:PORT behaviour, so nothing here
#  affects local dev.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The port this app should listen on. On Webuzo this is whatever port
# Application Manager auto-assigns the app (Admin > Settings > General >
# "Enduser Application(s) Settings" controls the assignable range).
# PORT=

# The public https URL for each of the 4 backends — every calculator page and
# the hub embed each other's origin (iframe src, API base, postMessage
# allow-list), so each one needs to know all four real addresses, not just
# its own. Set the same 4 values on every app.
#
# Option 1 — one app per backend, 4 subdomains (server/care_server.js,
# niva_server.js, mc_server.js, sh_server.js each deployed and run separately):
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_CARE=https://hub.yourdomain.com
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_NIVA=https://niva.yourdomain.com
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_MC=https://mc.yourdomain.com
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_STAR=https://star.yourdomain.com
#
# Option 2 (recommended for shared/panel-only hosting) — all 4 behind one
# process on one port (run server/combined_server.js instead of the 4
# individual servers): same domain for all four, with niva/mc/star suffixed
# by the path they're mounted at. Care stays at root (no suffix) since
# combined_server.js mounts it there.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_CARE=https://hub.yourdomain.com
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_NIVA=https://hub.yourdomain.com/niva
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_MC=https://hub.yourdomain.com/mc
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN_STAR=https://hub.yourdomain.com/star
